p('Periodic resetting, intermittent control, frame-average optimization and ongoing platform intervention are established. Our narrow contribution is a tight all-permitted-policy timing frontier for the SAME inherited cap in this lagged tolerance-guard model, paired with its finite-activation accounting and a separately certified playable game. The mechanism is a model-specific synthesis; the targeted literature review establishes neither first publication nor general controller optimality.')
p('Relevant primary sources: De Bruyne and Mori(2023), Physical Review Research 5,013122,doi:10.1103/PhysRevResearch.5.013122 (reset optimization); Liang and Xia(2020), Advances in Difference Equations 576,doi:10.1186/s13662-020-02969-3 (periodic intermittent control); Neely(2021), JMLR 22(279):1-44 (renewal reward/time objectives); Brero et al.(2022), NeurIPS 35, "Learning to Mitigate AI Collusion on Economic Platforms" (ongoing platform commitments). MacKay and Weinstein(2022), Washington University Law Review 100,111, "Dynamic Pricing Algorithms, Consumer Harm, and Regulatory Response," discusses algorithmic price regulation and timing. The separate close learned-policy audit by Lopes de Moraes and De Losso(2026), arXiv:2610.21867v2, prevents novelty claims about unilateral-DP/basin audits. Detailed source links and inspected sections are retained in the novelty notes.','Small')
p('All economic parameters, enforcement, symmetry and phase timing are known. No uncertainty in real demand or guard enforcement is included. A maximum-price stress path can be feasible without being stable against a seller\'s strategic deviation. No autonomous collusion discovery, incentive-compatible equilibrium, human comprehension, real-market welfare effect or adaptive-controller optimum is established. Cap-rule rate 1/K counts rule applications; it is not the fraction of quotes changed or a measured economic intervention cost. Profits on the worst-CS path are descriptive, not uniform seller-profit guarantees.')
p('The practical next checks are model-misspecification margins and whether the adverse script is attractive to individually optimizing sellers. Neither is answered by drawing another permitted path. The finite/continuous distinction, one-time/recurring distinction and individual-round/activation-average distinction remain explicit throughout the evidence.')
